test interpret
test run
target scry32

; Several values flying in parallel beyond the 1023 reference units a single
; `echo.l` output reference can express: `v0`, `v2` and `v3` are received at
; function entry and only consumed after a chain of 410 `iconst`/`iadd` pairs
; on `v1` (each pair is 5 reference units, so the chain spans 2050 units),
; which needs two chained long echoes per value. The bridges of one value
; lengthen the flight of the others, which the compiler must leave room for.
; The three values are consumed by non-commutative `isub`s in an order that
; differs from their arrival, so a misrouted or lost value changes the result.

function %far_parallel(i32 sext, i32 sext, i32 sext, i32 sext) -> i32 sext {
block0(v0: i32, v1: i32, v2: i32, v3: i32):
    v4 = iconst.i32 0x12345678
    v5 = iadd v1, v4
    v6 = iconst.i32 0x12345678
    v7 = iadd v5, v6
